              <items count="3">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">0cfa1b98-835b-45e0-b75c-c575ce010dab</item>
                <item name="Lib" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">6b0b6c1e-3f0a-4c55-9a43-2f7d4c1f8a10</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Shell BESO</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="5">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Bi-directional evolutionary structural optimisation of a shell for minimum compliance (maximum stiffness), including self-weight.
Mode 0 = Thickness: graded wall thickness, no holes (always printable). By default it keeps the clay volume of the Shell Model thickness and only redistributes it.
Mode 1 = Void: classic BESO, removes faces to make perforations.
Set Run to true (Boolean Toggle) to iterate. Set Reset to true to start over.
Connect the Design output to Print Layers (and to Shell Analysis to analyse the result).</item>
                    <item name="Hidden" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
